      "writtenOn": "2022-03-25T20:31:30Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Thanks for the context, Romain!\n\nGiven that there isn\u0027t a single SDK, will we (eventually) also need to migrate information about the sdk version? e.g.\n* `ContactsProvider` has `platform_apis: true`\n* `SystemUI-tags` uses the current sdk \n* `framework-minus-apex` has `sdk_version: \"core_platform\"`\n\nWill we need to migrate other properties for the `event_log_tags` library target (e.g. `javacflags` or whether optimization is enabled)?\n\nMy light preference would be for our rule to only generate the `.java` files to use as an input in `srcs` as it doesn\u0027t require migrating additional properties or creating macros for multiple module types.\n\nBut we can also reevaluate after considering:\n* which/how many properties additional will need to migrate\n* whether we need to support multiple rules (e.g. `java_library`, `android_library`, `droidstubs`).\n\nAlso in a separate CL (low priority), can we move `build/make/tools/event_log_tags.bzl` to `build/bazel/rules` with the remaining build rules we\u0027ve written?",
